# The lift dispatcher with three stops. Call buttons for Ground, Middle
# and Top are on the computer's left, right and front; the send outputs
# are colours of bundled cable on its back (white, orange, magenta), as
# they would run to Create elevator contacts or train station links.
# Top has an arrived input: a lever on top of the computer stands in
# for the contact that is on while the car is there. The other stops
# are reached by travel time (4 s a stop).
name Lift dispatcher
description A lift controller with call buttons left (Ground), right (Middle) and front (Top), send outputs on bundled cable at the back, and a lever on top as Top's arrived contact. Monitor: monitor_0.
description The timeline sets up the stops at the prompt, calls Top at 5 s, then Ground and Middle while the car is on its way; the lever says it reached Top at 12 s. With look it serves Middle before Ground.

ground -6 -6 6 6 0 3 ores=false pockets=false
block -1 0 1 button
block 1 0 1 button
block 0 1 1 button
block 0 0 2 lever
fill 0 -1 0 0 -3 0 bundled_cable

computer 1 Lift
  pos 0 0 1
  heading north
  peripheral monitor_0 monitor size=3x2 at=-2,3,1
  autorun lift monitor_0

at 1 type 1 stop Ground left back:white
at 1.5 type 1 unstop Top
at 2 type 1 stop Middle right back:orange
at 2.5 type 1 stop Top front back:magenta top
at 5 press 0 1 1
at 6 press -1 0 1
at 7 press 1 0 1
at 12 toggle 0 0 2

check calls are queued and Middle is served before Ground
  seconds 20
  expect log stop 3 Top: call front, send back:magenta, arrived top
  expect log sent to Top from Ground (back:magenta pulse)
  expect log call at Ground (queue: Ground)
  expect log call at Middle (queue: Ground, Middle)
  expect log at Top
  expect log sent to Middle from Top
  expect not log sent to Ground
  expect screen 1 Queue: Ground
  expect no-error

check the car ends up back at Ground with the queue empty
  seconds 32
  expect log sent to Ground from Middle
  expect log at Ground (by travel time)
  expect log waiting at Ground
  expect screen 1 Queue: empty
  expect no-error
